WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One of the characters,
who's fantastic

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.836
and is one of the professional
skateboarders in his first film,

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:04.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
his character's name --
and, obviously,

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:06.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
this is gonna get beeped
for broadcast --

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:08.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
is [bleep]
-Yeah.

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:08.608 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:09.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And can you explain --
-F-S.

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:12.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
Can you explain how he --

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:15.315
It's such a wonderful detail
as to why that's his nickname.

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:18.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because anytime
he sees something he likes,

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:20.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
he yells out, "[Bleep]
That was dope."

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.156 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:24.491 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's a good --

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:26.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
You actually -- You did work
at a skateboard shop

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:27.627 size:75% position:38% line:92%
when you were young?

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:32.265
-I spent a lot of time at a shop
called Hot Rod in West L.A.,

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:33.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is now, I think,
a barbershop,

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:35.969 size:75% position:38%
and for some reason,
they kept the name.

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:37.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And so, it sucks,

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:39.305 size:75% position:38%
because so many kids
grew up going there

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.541
and, like, spending their youth
at this place,

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:44.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
and now it's a barbershop,
and it's weird.

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:47.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, but, yeah.
I mean, it was a great place.

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:51.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
I learned a lot of amazing
and terrible lessons,

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:56.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I found people
that I really related to,

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:59.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, honestly,
it gave me this lens

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:02.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I kind of think
I really do see life through,

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:04.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
like a certain taste,
a certain --

00:01:04.264 --> 00:01:06.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, there was a magazine
called "Big Brother"

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:10.103
that was such a subversive
sense of humor, you know?

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:11.237 line:92%
That "Jackass" came out of.

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:16.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know, just taste
in music, in hip-hop and punk,

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:18.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
and sort of the way
that young people

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.180 size:75% position:38%
dealt with authority
was very different

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:24.117
in this group of gentlemen than
it was in other parts of life.

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:27.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
And for whatever reason,
it spoke to me,

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:31.357 size:78% position:39%
and I'm no ambassador
for skateboarding.

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:33.326 line:92%
I'm not an authority on it.

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:36.596 line:92%
But I'm a nerd who loves it

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:40.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
and wanted
to see it honored onscreen.

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:44.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You also wrote a magazine
that is a companion,

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:45.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess, to the film.
-Definitely.

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:47.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And this is --
you interviewed 12 people

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:50.877
that you love and respect
about being that age, yeah?

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:53.847
-Yeah, it's basically
a companion piece to the movie,

00:01:53.847 --> 00:01:56.616
a magazine I made with A24,
called "Inner Children."

00:01:56.616 --> 00:02:02.055
And the movie, at its core,
is about this kid who's lonely,

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:04.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he finds
his group of people.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:07.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
Really,
it's about self-acceptance.

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:08.528 line:92%
So, basically, his currency

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:10.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
is getting the [bleep]
kicked out of him

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:11.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
and taking abuse
and taking hits,

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:14.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
whether it's on a skateboard,
at home, to himself.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:17.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
I don't want to give it away,

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:20.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
but the journey
is self-acceptance

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.407 line:92%
and self-love, essentially.

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:23.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I wrote this magazine
because I believe

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:28.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
everybody has
this snapshot of themselves.

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:30.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's a snapshot
that they kind of

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:31.484 line:92%
want to hide from the world.

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:35.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so mine was, like,
being this, like, 14-year-old,

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:38.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
overweight kid, kind of
feeling ugly to the world,

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:41.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
wanting to fit in with
this group of skateboarders,

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:44.664
and I kind of feel like,
even if that's not yours,

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:47.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
that every person has one
of these they can relate to.

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:50.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I interviewed
a lot of my heroes --

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:51.604 line:92%
my sister, Beanie Feldstein,

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:54.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
from "Lady Bird"
and "Hello, Dolly!"

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:56.409 line:92%
DJ Premier, Behati Prinsloo,

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:58.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
Edie Falco,
Kim Gordon from Sonic Youth,

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:02.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
Mark Gonzalez, Michael Cera,
Na-kel Smith, Q-Tip,

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:05.652
Raymond Pettibon, a lot of
my favorite artists and people,

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:08.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was so meaningful
to find out

00:03:08.288 --> 00:03:11.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
that peoples
are completely different,

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:13.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
but they hurt just as much.
-Sure.

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:18.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And so it was just a nice
kind of liberating way

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:21.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
to spend these last few years
figuring out

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:26.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
who I am as a person,
how do you love yourself,

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:27.607 line:92%
and how do you be yourself

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:30.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
and be the artist that you are
without apologizing for it.

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:33.112
And what came out
was this magazine and "Mid90s,"

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:34.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I hope
you enjoy both of them.

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:37.317 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:40.820 line:92%
-You have long been an artist --

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:41.688 line:92%
You've long been an artist

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:43.523 size:81% position:41%
that people have been
inspired by your work.

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:45.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did not realize
the level of inspiration.

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:47.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've posted
a few of these on Instagram.

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:50.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
People have gotten
Jonah Hill tattoos.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:51.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:03:51.698 --> 00:03:52.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And now, I think,
when I say that,

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:55.535
you're picturing something,
and it's a lot more intense

00:03:55.535 --> 00:03:58.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
than even what
you're picturing.

00:03:58.037 --> 00:04:01.374 line:92%
So this is what somebody did.

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:02.475 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, that's --

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:03.142 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Audience groans ]

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:05.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think that's
the perfect comment to write,

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:08.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
which you just wrote, "Okay."
-Yeah.

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:08.748 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:11.618
-But how about this gentleman
that wants to go through life

00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:13.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
with that on his --
[ Audience groans ]

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:15.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Again, I was very clever.
I wrote, "Okay."

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:16.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:18.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, I think that would be
what you would say

00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:19.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
if somebody came up to you,
was like,

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:20.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Jonah, I want to show you
something really cool."

00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:25.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean it's a little better
that they're characters

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:28.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
as opposed to me just, like,
chilling.

00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:30.303 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:32.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-And it's -- yeah.

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:35.575
I really don't know how to feel,
to be honest with you.

00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:37.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:38.911 line:92%
-I feel honored and weird,

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:44.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I hope
you enjoy my face forever.

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:46.919 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:49.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know what?
For the first time in my life,

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:51.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
I enjoy having
my face on me forever,

00:04:51.224 --> 00:04:52.125 line:92%
so I think you can have --

00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:53.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go, yeah.
Give it up.

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:55.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
Spread the wealth.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:57.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
Last but not least,
you are gonna host --

00:04:57.897 --> 00:05:00.466
Next week, you're hosting "SNL"
for the fifth time.

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:01.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-That is fantastic.

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:03.569 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:06.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was there your first time.
-Yes, you were.

00:05:06.406 --> 00:05:09.709
-And a character of yours
that still, to this day,

00:05:09.709 --> 00:05:10.710 line:92%
is one of my favorite things

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:12.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I ever was lucky enough
to work on.

00:05:12.679 --> 00:05:15.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
You played Adam Grossman,
who is a 6-year-old.

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:19.686
There he is with his dad,
Bill Hader, at a Benihana,

00:05:19.686 --> 00:05:21.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he's --
-Yeah, and you --

00:05:21.521 --> 00:05:22.655 line:92%
And Bill and I got to write

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:24.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
the first one of those
we did together.

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:26.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, he was just a very
precocious 6-year-old

00:05:26.893 --> 00:05:28.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
who sounded like
a very old Jewish man.

00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:32.165 size:84% position:42%
-Yeah. So, essentially,
Hader was telling us

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:34.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
a story about --
in his hometown,

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:36.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
he went to Benihana,
and he saw a kid,

00:05:36.803 --> 00:05:39.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
but he didn't know if
it was like a 40-year-old man

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:43.509
or a 6-year-old kid, because
he had a velour tracksuit on,

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:45.411 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and when the chef did --

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:46.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm getting so many laughs
off Bill's bit.

00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:50.783
But when the chef did the trick,
the kid just went --

00:05:50.783 --> 00:05:52.085 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Clapping ]

00:05:52.085 --> 00:05:52.618 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.618 --> 00:05:55.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, I think Bill
started doing him

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:57.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
as a Mafia, like,
Tony Soprano guy.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:06:00.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you were there!
And then, I started doing him

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:03.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
as, like, a Catskills --
-Yeah, he was very Catskill.

00:06:03.996 --> 00:06:05.598 line:92%
-Like super-hacky Catskills.

00:06:05.598 --> 00:06:08.368
And then you, Bill, and I
stayed up all night writing it,

00:06:08.368 --> 00:06:09.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we were laughing.
-It was great.

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:11.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was one of the joyous
memories of my life.

00:06:11.471 --> 00:06:12.205 size:75% position:38% line:92%
It was a great time.

00:06:12.205 --> 00:06:15.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And the best moment of it
was his catchphrase

00:06:15.375 --> 00:06:16.776 line:92%
if he had one was, "I'm 6."

00:06:16.776 --> 00:06:17.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think
he would definitely have --

00:06:17.944 --> 00:06:20.313
say he had a catchphrase,
'cause he shouted it out.

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:22.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But the genius
that you added to it was,

00:06:22.115 --> 00:06:24.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
he didn't quite hold up
his six fingers

00:06:24.317 --> 00:06:26.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the confidence
that he said "I'm 6."

00:06:26.219 --> 00:06:29.021
Can you give us a little of
the Adam Grossman fingers?

00:06:29.021 --> 00:06:31.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, 'cause, little kids,
they like --

00:06:31.157 --> 00:06:34.794
they, like, hold up their hands.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:34.794 --> 00:06:37.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or, like, they --
They, like, don't do it right.

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:41.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was my favorite detail
of the character.

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:42.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm so happy
to see you back on the show.

00:06:42.802 --> 00:06:44.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, man, it is great
to have you here, as well.

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:47.774 size:81% position:41%
Congrats on the movie.
Jonah Hill, everybody.

